Package: drawn
Title: Design-Based Sampling with Known Inclusion Probabilities
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Justin", "Chase", email = "jchase.msu@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Draws probability samples from data frames under an explicit,
    reusable sampling design: simple random, stratified, systematic, cluster,
    multi-stage, weighted (including probability-proportional-to-size),
    reservoir, bootstrap, temporal and spatial. A design is a value that can be
    stored, printed and reused, and that knows its own first- and second-order
    inclusion probabilities, so a drawn sample carries the weights needed for
    Horvitz-Thompson estimation and 'ht_total()' returns a population total
    with a standard error and confidence interval. Designs whose inclusion
    probabilities have no closed form report that rather than supplying an
    approximation, and can be estimated by simulation instead.
